    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200-a4">

                <pb facs="0299" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg225"/>

                <head>Mr. Van Valkenburgh to Major Murray.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 22, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of the 18th instant, informing me that you have been
                    instructed to pay to the representative of the United States the sum of eleven
                    thousand six hundred and sixty-six dollars and sixty-six cents, ($11,666 66,)
                    being the amount received into the treasury chest at Yokohama in excess of the
                    proportion due to her Majesty’s government of the second and third instalments
                    of the Japanese indemnity. I will call at your office, or send an order, for the
                    check soon.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the
                            United States in Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Major <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. W. Murray,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Commissariat General, Yokohama.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
